CORES Database

Comments:
The Cores database contains 2636 cores of protein element ORFs encoded by the different MGEs analyzed in second GyDB release GyDB 2.0. It also includes a set of core protein domains identified in a variety of integrase-transposase like enzymes (GIN/GINGER TRs and INTs)

The sequences are labeled and in fasta format. Labels are prefixed by the protein abbreviation (below you have the mean of all abbreviations) and suffixed by the element name. Some ORFs correspond to accessory genes of Retroviridae and Caulimoviridae species. Note that many may have the same or a similar name (for instance ORF II, ORFX etc) but this does not necessarily mean a counterpart relationship. 

